  few years but in order to get to being a  developed economy  me what you need more of in China is  consumption people spending money again  there's a difference between the surface  the smart shops in Chengdu and the  reality Beijing seems reluctant to  encourage more consumer spending  maybe it's because when households spend  and earn more they tend to want more  democracy and that is China's real  dilemma it's getting to the stage where  it may only be able to sustain its  growth by changing its political system  for the leaders in Beijing that is an  unappetizing prospect if anything  president G is actually clamping down  more than his predecessors especially in  Xinjiang province whether Muslim  minority resents Beijing's control in  Hong Kong this time last year a change  of stance on direct elections spot  protests that went off for months for  many China watchers it's all part of one  big story they say either the communist  leaders embrace democracy willingly or  they watch their economy slump and maybe  lose control altogether ed Conway's Sky  News in China
 

